CAPI=2:

name: ::rc_core:1.0.0
description: >
  RC-owned RTL for Commit 2a: the PG213 <-> Transaction Layer bridge. 2a-0 is
  the pair of descriptor-agnostic AXI-Stream width gearboxes converting between
  the 128-bit PG213 user interface and the TL's 32-bit Dword-serial
  command/payload port. 2a-i adds pcie_rq_rc_pkg (PG213 descriptor types, owned
  here -- tlp_pkg stays untouched) and pcie_rq_if, the Requester Request slave.
  From 2a-i on this core depends on ::tlp_core, because pcie_rq_if drives the
  TL's tlp_cmd_e command port and reuses tlp_pkg's byte-enable functions to
  check that the byte enables it forwards are ones the TL can reproduce. 2a-ii
  adds pcie_rc_if, the Requester Completion master: it registers the parsed
  completion header into alignment with the request tracker's one-cycle-later
  result digest, builds the 96-bit RC descriptor, and streams it ahead of the
  payload through pcie_axis_dw_upsize. 2a-iii adds pcie_rq_rc_top, which is
  wiring only: pcie_rq_if + tlp_layer + pcie_rc_if behind the PG213 user
  interface. It EXPOSES link_up_i / transmit_enable_i / fc_initialized_i /
  fc_update_valid_i, because tlp_layer emits nothing and reports nothing
  without all four, and it ties off the Completer (CQ/CC) surface, which is the
  endpoint side and out of scope for Commit 2a. 2b-3 adds pcie_enum_top, also
  wiring only: it now owns the ONE pcie_cfg_txn on behalf of every enumeration
  stage, so pcie_enum_scan no longer instantiates the primitive and carries no
  parameters at all. The hoist is behaviour-neutral -- pcie_enum_scan's
  sequencer body is byte-identical across it -- and exists so that pcie_enum_bar
  can share the primitive instead of duplicating it, which keeps
  single-outstanding a property of the netlist rather than of an FSM's good
  behaviour.

filesets:
  rtl:
    depend:
      - ::tlp_core:1.0.0
      - fusesoc:pcie:dllp_core:1.0.0
      - fusesoc:pcie:lint
    files:
      - pcie_axis_dw_downsize.sv
      - pcie_axis_dw_upsize.sv
      - pcie_rq_rc_pkg.sv
      - pcie_enum_pkg.sv
      - pcie_rq_if.sv
      - pcie_rc_if.sv
      - pcie_cq_if.sv
      - pcie_rq_rc_top.sv
      - pcie_rc_dl_top.sv
      - pcie_cfg_txn.sv
      - pcie_enum_scan.sv
      - pcie_enum_bar.sv
      - pcie_enum_bus.sv
      - pcie_enum_top.sv
      - pcie_enum_dl_top.sv
    file_type: systemVerilogSource

targets:
  default:
    filesets:
      - rtl
